course: dictionary
lesson: 10791
title: Vandal: a word with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vandal is a person who deliberately damages or destroys property. Deliberately means on purpose, so a vandal breaks things because they want to, not by accident. Property means things that belong to people or to the public, like windows, benches and walls.
explain: Context gives you the clue. Vandals break windows or spray graffiti, so a vandal wrecks or defaces things. Vandalism is the act itself, and it is a crime. Try your meaning in a sentence: «The park bench was smashed by vandals» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Look at the capital letter. In «many peoples pushing across its borders, such as Goths, Vandals and Huns», the word Vandals has a capital V, because it is the name of a group of people. Here it is not a person who damages things. Capital letters are a clue too.
fact: A vandal is a person who deliberately damages or destroys property.
fact: Vandalism is the crime of damaging property on purpose, such as breaking windows or spraying graffiti.
fact: Phrases you may see are «vandals broke» the windows, or a place was «attacked by vandals».
fact: «The Vandals», with a capital V, were a group of people who attacked Rome long ago.
fact: In the western empire, many problems together weakened Rome, not one single cause, and the Vandals were one of the peoples pushing across its borders.
exercise: «The vandals broke the bus shelter window last night.» What is a vandal? | A person who lives in a shelter | A person who sells glass | A person who cleans up parks | *A person who deliberately damages or destroys property
exercise: «The Vandals were one of the peoples pushing across the borders of Rome.» What does the capital V show? | It starts a new sentence only | It is a spelling mistake | *It is the name of a group of people | It means something is broken
exercise: Asha says spraying graffiti on a wall is just a bit of fun. Why is vandalism a crime? | *Because it deliberately damages property that belongs to other people | Because it only happens at night | Because it is always done by adults | Because it makes the streets look clean
test: «Vandals smashed the playground swings.» What does vandals mean here? | Children who are playing | Animals that climb on the frame | Workers who fix the swings | *People who deliberately damage property
test: «The old town was attacked by vandals long ago.» Which word tells you vandals are people who damage things? | *attacked | long | old | town
exam: Jayden reads that «the Vandals attacked Rome», then reads that «vandals broke the bus shelter». Which statement is correct? | *The capital V names a group of people, and the small v means a person who damages property | Both mean exactly the same thing, with no difference at all | Neither word has a meaning, so you should skip them | The capital V means a shelter, and the small v means a park
